meta {
  name: Label Kinship Chain
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/kinship/label
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "steps": ["father", "brother", "son"]
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.label_fa: eq پسرعمو
  res.body.label_en: isString
}

docs {
  # Label Kinship Chain

  Public, no account. Names the relation reached by walking `steps` from the speaker, using the same labeller as the relationship finder. Steps: `father`, `mother`, `son`, `daughter`, `brother`, `sister`, `husband`, `wife`; 1 to 8 of them. Starting with `wife` or `husband` also tells the labeller the speaker's gender, which in-law names depend on (پدرزن vs پدرشوهر).

  Rate-limited per IP (`KINSHIP_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE`).

  The descriptions spell out the graph hops, so a brother or sister shows as a parent and then a child.

  ## Output `200`
  ```json
  {
    "label_fa": "پسرعمو",
    "label_en": "paternal uncle's son",
    "description_fa": "پسرِ پسرِ والدِ پدر",
    "description_en": "father's parent's son's son"
  }
  ```
}
